    "body": "Successor program to #399 (falsifier-2 record complete there). Established facts: on broad-topic corpora (wiki10k and its 500k subsample) the substrate scores ~26-27% at EVERY measured capacity (starved 26.1, subsample 26.0, ratio-scaled 26.5 with a healthy 69-node cover); the fwd-anchor channel inverts regardless of capacity; EXCT precedence is mildly negative under diversity (Rule 1 27.1 > Rule 1+2 26.5); the 36.5-era positives are redundancy-regime records. Open questions: (1) what carries the remaining ~73% — is the ceiling evidence-sparsity (most held-out contexts genuinely novel at this corpus size) or representation (codes/cover can't separate diverse contexts)? (2) does the EXCT-precedence sign flip warrant a diversity-conditional Rule 2 gate? (3) capacity sweep shape: entropy-floor (R4_COVER_ENTROPY_GAIN_BITS) and depth sweeps are now cheap via #432's env knobs. First measurement candidate: evidence-sparsity audit — for held-out misses, does the construction split contain ANY matching evidence at any key (upper bound on what better representation could recover)?",
